  10: [['MACK', 'The Deacon\'s gone grey. The choir\'s scattered. And Dottie\'s name was on the sign-up sheet in lipstick, with a little heart. Little hearts are never good news.'], ['SALLY', 'We\'ll get her back, Mack. Tomorrow. Tonight we drink to her. Gus! Something rye! In a martini glass! For Dottie!']],
  11: [['MACK', 'Dottie\'s home. Dented, sober, and wearing a tin-foil halo she refuses to take off. She says she saw a door under the city. I believe her. That\'s the scary part.'], ['DOTTIE', '*hic* Gus! I\'m back! I\'m a lapsed prophet! What\'s good for that?'], ['SALLY', 'EVERYTHING, Dottie. Everything\'s good for that. Gus, line \'em up for the robot.']],
